## Context

PR #493 re-pointed `scripts/projects.json` after the 2026-07 home
reorganization moved every project out of `~`. Review during that PR's
verification found stale pre-reorg `~/<name>` paths in files outside that
PR's logical unit — the nightbeat registry was fixed, but hardcoded paths
elsewhere still point at the old locations.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/setup-claude-agent.sh:8-11` — hardcoded PROJECTS array
  (`~/cadens`, `~/Climate_finance`, `~/aedist-technical-report`,
  `~/fuzzy-corpus`)
- `skills/maw-audit/SKILL.md:109-110` and `:212-215` — operator launch
  paths (`~/git-erg`, `~/aedist-technical-report`)
- `STATE.md:29` — `~/aedist-technical-report` in an active directive
- `skills/scry/SKILL.md` — pre-existing internal path inconsistency, verify
  while there

## Actions

1. Re-point each stale path to its post-reorg location. Verify each target
   with `git -C <path> remote get-url origin` before editing.
2. Confirm no other pre-reorg `~/<name>` project path survives in the tree.

## Verification

- [ ] Each listed path resolves to a live checkout at its post-reorg location
- [ ] `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes

## Exit criteria

- No pre-reorg `~/<name>` project path remains in the listed files
- `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes
